  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "application-glycomics-massmatchr-01d4",
  "summary": "Recent preprints apply LLM agents to proteomics, transcriptomics, gene-level evidence, and literature-derived databases with traceable outputs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is LLM-mediated access to domain computational resources, with emphasis on auditability. The proteomics agent framework pairs conversational querying of LC-MS/MS datasets with executable checks, controls, and traceable decisions. GLESKit links gene-level databases, tools, and literature through MCP into retained workspaces that yield reviewable reports. ProtoPure uses an LLM-based workflow to extract 12 standardized purification parameters from literature across UniProt proteomes. A benchmark of LLMs and agentic coding systems addresses automated transcriptomic analysis and visualization of COVID-19 host responses. Other items are non-agentic tool or infrastructure papers: BaitBench, tWhEEL, a random forest model for differential protein-protein interactions, SiSaNA, the dictyBase reimplementation, and PoolParty. What is distinctive in the agentic items is the focus on checkable outputs, via executable controls, retained workspaces, and reviewable reports, rather than agent capability alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
